  <h2 id="r6-resolutions">Round 6 Findings Closed in <code>v2.5.0-rfc</code></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>R6-H1 (Slashing Predicate Bypass):</strong> <code>SubmitInvalidCertProof(cert)</code> now verifies the
      BLS12-381 aggregate signature under the <strong>historical Tag-15 committee matching
      <code>cert.FinalityCommitteeRoot</code></strong> (rather than <code>canonicalSigningCommitteeRoot(cert.Height)</code>),
      then evaluates all 7 certificate fields against canonical state. <code>CarryOverCertificate</code> is deleted,
      and the handoff pin is honestly specified as economically enforced via Zenon slashing rather than an in-circuit
      oracle.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>R6-H2 &amp; R6-M1 (Leaf-3B W-OTS Granularity &amp; Fixed 408 B Encoding):</strong> Certificate DA is now
      encoded as a fixed 408 B two-slot payload (<code>targetCert || handoffSlot</code>, zero-padded to 204 zero bytes
      for 1-cert epochs) committed as <strong>7 independent per-block checksummed <code>OP_HASH160</code> W-OTS
      messages</strong> + 6 midstates (<code>1,239</code> digits, <code>29,882 vB &rarr; 30 kvB</code>, Leaf-3B peak
      <code>265</code> digits = <code>530</code> witness elements leaving <code>470</code> free under 1,000,
      <code>C = 1,208</code>).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>R6-M2 (Latency-Aware Reachability &amp; Reservations):</strong> <code>RequestPegOut</code>,
      <code>ClaimFrontingSlot</code>, and <code>MINTED_LOCK_V1</code> evaluate <code>ReachableRounds</code> at
      <code>now + 3.0d</code>, reserve lane rounds per active slot, and permit <code>0x0D</code> re-graphing on
      un-claimed <code>RELEASED</code> vaults.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>R6-M3 (Decoupled Release Proof):</strong> <code>BTC_RELEASE_PROOF</code> always admits valid fronting
      payments even if another operator's substitution trapped the assigned vault, paired with permissionless
      <code>RepointTrappedPegOut</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>R6-M4 &amp; R6-M5 (Single-Authority Anti-Censorship Fronting Slots):</strong> Settlement and domain agree
      on both Zenon time and Bitcoin height expiry; <code>MINTED_RELEASE_V1</code> keys strictly on the domain winner;
      slots lock a forfeitable <code>500 ZNN</code> <code>SlotBondZnn</code> and bar consecutive re-claim by
      <code>lastLapsedOperatorId</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>R6-L1..L9 &amp; S6-1..S6-6:</strong> Aligned <code>OP_HASH160</code> across prose &amp; oracle, added
      strict duplicate/3rd-epoch rejection in <code>0x0D</code>, exact <code>unrotatedVaultCount</code> inc/dec via
      <code>quarantineReason</code>, <code>+60h</code> finalization grace before quarantine, published Take-txid leaf
      DA + raw-sweep halting across <code>ACTIVE</code>/<code>RELEASED</code>/<code>QUARANTINED</code>, exact
      <code>anchorExpiryTs == finalityEpochStartTs(epoch) + 58d</code> equality, distinct IETF BLS POP DSTs + depth-5
      SHA-256 committee tree + inner STARK / outer Groth16 split, <code>ResetFailedReimbursementSlot</code> +
      <code>1.476x</code>/<code>1.591x</code> slow-block tolerance disclosures, and 180-day timeline simulation in
      <code>scripts/verify_spec_bounds.py</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>

